## Origin

2026-08-19 — operator hard rule. Recorded alongside the nav-crawl work:
heuristic readiness waits (`networkidle`, fixed sleeps, content markers)
were a primary cause of a ~2 minute sweep degrading to hours, and of
pages being "verified" while broken or still loading. Three-state
requirement exists so `error` cannot satisfy a ready wait.
